---
import type {RevisedCapability} from '../data/capabilityRedesign';
import {prototypeApproval} from '../data/capabilityRedesign';
import PentaInnerHero from './PentaInnerHero.astro';
import CapabilityReference from './CapabilityReference.astro';
import CapabilityEvidence from './CapabilityEvidence.astro';
import CapabilityInquiry from './CapabilityInquiry.astro';
import {libraryGuide} from '../data/resourceLibrary';
import '../styles/prototype-machining.css';
interface Props {page:RevisedCapability;quoteHref:string}
const {page,quoteHref}=Astro.props;
const cooling={...page.parts[1],text:'Intake and cooling interfaces for prototype fit checks. Define joints and any supplied-part scope.'};
const throttle={...page.parts[2],text:'Bores, mounting and actuator interfaces for development checks.'};
const materialLinks=[['Aluminum','aluminum-cnc-parts'],['Stainless steel','stainless-steel-cnc-parts'],['Copper & brass','copper-brass-cnc-parts'],['Engineering plastics','plastic-machined-parts']];
---
<div class="prototype-page pn-capability-rollout" data-penta-capability={page.slug}>
 <PentaInnerHero title={page.plan.title} lead="Check fit, assembly or appearance on a CNC-machined prototype before committing to the next revision or batch." slug={page.slug} part={page.parts[0]} quoteHref={quoteHref} secondaryHref="#part-examples" secondaryLabel="Plan the evaluation"/>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-scope" id="part-examples" data-core-section="evaluation-scope"><header><h2>What does the prototype need to prove?</h2><p>We plan the build around your evaluation. Mark the fixed interfaces, mounting datums, clearances and cover fits.</p></header><div class="prototype-references"><CapabilityReference part={cooling} namedLink singleEntry/><CapabilityReference part={throttle} namedLink singleEntry/></div><div class="prototype-application"><h3>Automotive &amp; motorcycle prototypes</h3><div><p>Agree pressure, functional or vehicle tests separately, including procedures, fixtures, limits and who validates the result.</p></div></div></section>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-approval" id="engineering-fit" data-core-section="approval-record"><header><h2>Keep the revision, checks and approval together</h2></header><table class="rd-table rd-stacked"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Input</th><th scope="col">Method & responsibility</th><th scope="col">Reviewable result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{prototypeApproval.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.stage}</th><td data-label="Input">{row.input}</td><td data-label="Method & responsibility">{row.method}</td><td data-label="Reviewable result">{row.result}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><div class="prototype-approval-evidence pi-inspection-pair"><CapabilityEvidence id="cmm-room" caption="Original LZZ CMM photograph." sizes="(max-width:767px) calc(100vw - 90px), 400px"/><div><h3>Checks for the prototype</h3><p>We agree the features, methods and report before machining, and review current equipment calibration evidence.</p><a class="rd-link" href={libraryGuide('machined-prototype-approval-checklist').href}>Prototype approval checklist</a></div></div></section>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-differences" id="materials-finishes" data-core-section="production-differences"><header><h2>Record what differs from production</h2><p>An approved substitute can suit the prototype but may limit what it proves about the production part.</p></header><dl><div><dt>Material and condition</dt><dd>Record changes in alloy, temper, polymer grade, fillers and stock condition. For 6061 or 7075, match temper and heat treatment to the evaluation and production specification, with the required material records.</dd></div><div><dt>Finish and working surfaces</dt><dd>Record both finishes. Protect fits, contacts and threads, and set dimensions after treatment.</dd></div><div><dt>Edges and measurement state</dt><dd>Agree burr limits, edge quality, cleaning and measurement conditions. Flag tests that need the production material or finish.</dd></div></dl><nav class="prototype-material-links" aria-label="Material selection">{materialLinks.map(([title,slug])=><a class="rd-link" href={'/capabilities/'+slug+'/'}>{title}</a>)}</nav><div class="prototype-next"><h3>The next revision or batch</h3><div><p>Acceptance applies only to the tested revision and scope. Record issues and approve changes before cutting again; a batch needs its own revision, quantity, sampling plan and order.</p><nav aria-label="Next production steps"><a class="rd-link" href="/capabilities/low-volume-production/">Plan the first batch</a><a class="rd-link" href="/about/how-we-work/">Project responsibilities</a></nav></div></div></section>
 <CapabilityInquiry page={page} quoteHref={quoteHref} title="Request a prototype review" orderFirst coreSection="quotation"/>
</div>
